      "priority": 4,
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Added COUNTER_MAP (13 entries: revive, heal, bleed, disrupted, slow, blind, offense_down, defense_down, stun, ability_block, taunt, dispel, counter_attack) with weights 5–12 to src/lib/tower-scoring-data.ts. Added counterScore(teamTags, opponentTags, counterMap=COUNTER_MAP) to src/lib/tower-scoring.ts — earned/maxWeight ratio scaled to 0–100, de-dupes opponent tags, ignores unknown opp tags. 9 new tests in src/lib/tower-scoring.test.ts (now 17 total) — all pass. Typecheck + ESLint clean for the 3 touched files (pre-existing lint errors elsewhere are unrelated)."
    },
    {
      "id": "US-005",
      "title": "roleBalanceScore pure function",
      "description": "As the solver, I need a small bonus for teams with healer + tank + ≥2 damage so a balanced kit beats a pure-DPS stack when other scores are equal.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/lib/tower-scoring.ts exports roleBalanceScore(teamTags: Record<string, string[]>): number returning 0–100",
        "Roles inferred from tag presence: healer (heal), tank (taunt OR defense_up), disruptor (ability_block OR stun OR disrupted), damage (default for any character without healer/tank tags)",
        "Returns 100 when team has ≥1 healer, ≥1 tank or disruptor, ≥2 damage; scales down proportionally",
        "Pure: no IO",
        "Unit tests cover: all-damage team, healer-only team, balanced team, full-tank team",
        "Tests pass",
        "Typecheck passes"
      ],
      "priority": 5,
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Added roleBalanceScore(teamTags) to src/lib/tower-scoring.ts. Score = sum of 3 components × (100/3): healer present (heal tag), frontline present (taunt/defense_up OR ability_block/stun/disrupted), damage count (min(damage,2)/2). Damage bucket excludes characters with healer/tank tags per PRD AC. Fully balanced team (≥1 healer, ≥1 frontline, ≥2 damage) → 100. Single-role teams → ~33. Empty team → 0. 8 new tests in tower-scoring.test.ts (33 total) — all pass. Typecheck + ESLint clean. Note: PRD AC mentioned `defense_up` for tank role but it's not in ABILITY_TAG_VOCABULARY; included it in TANK_TAGS for forward-compat — only `taunt` actually matches today."
    },
    {
      "id": "US-006",
      "title": "Blend composite score into solveTowerAllocation",
      "description": "As a commander, I want the tower planner to pick the team with the highest composite score (not just highest power) among teams that pass the safety-margin gate.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "src/lib/tower-solver.ts uses composite = 0.45*powerMargin + 0.20*factionSynergy + 0.25*counter + 0.10*roleBalance",
        "Weights live as exported constants in src/lib/tower-scoring.ts (TOWER_SCORING_WEIGHTS) so they can be tuned",
        "Eligibility filter and safety-margin gate remain unchanged — composite only re-ranks teams that already pass the gate",
        "powerMarginScore normalized 0–100: 0 at margin 0%, 100 at margin ≥ 50% over safety threshold",
        "Opponent ability tags fetched once per /api/tower/solve request and passed into the solver",
        "Existing tower-solver unit tests still pass",
        "Typecheck passes",
        "Tests pass"
      ],
      "priority": 6,
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Added TOWER_SCORING_WEIGHTS, powerMarginScore, CompositeBreakdown, compositeScore to src/lib/tower-scoring.ts. Extended SolverOptions with opponentTags + characterTags + factionPassives; added optional compositeScore field to TeamAssignment. Composite re-ranking activates ONLY when characterTags is supplied AND the team passed the safety-margin gate (preserves US-003 behavior + back-compat for existing tests that pass no tags). Candidate enumeration uses combinations from the top-12 strongest eligible chars (C(12,5)=792 worst case). Tie-break: composite total → raw power. Route now collects opponent unit IDs + roster IDs, calls extractAbilityTags once, builds opponentTagsByRoom map, and passes everything to the solver. Added route mock for @/lib/tower-ability-tags. New tests: 7 in tower-scoring.test.ts (weights, powerMarginScore, compositeScore), 3 in tower-solver.test.ts (composite re-ranks counter team, back-compat without tags, margin-fallback skips composite). All pass; typecheck + ESLint clean."
    },
    {
      "id": "US-007",
      "title": "Composite-aware confidence labels + reason breakdown",
      "description": "As a commander, I want the 'Why this team?' expansion to break down the four sub-scores so I can tell whether a recommendation is truly strong or just high-power.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "TowerAssignment.reason includes a structured composite-score breakdown: power, synergy, counter, roleBalance, total (all 0–100)",
        "Confidence label derives from composite (not raw margin): ≥75 'Strong pick', 55–74 'Should work', 35–54 'Risky', <35 'Likely loss'",
        "TowerPlannerClient.tsx 'Why this team?' panel renders each sub-score on its own line with the human descriptions from FACTION_PASSIVES / COUNTER_MAP where applicable",
        "Existing tests for confidence label updated to reflect new thresholds",
        "Tests pass",
        "Typecheck passes"
